From 06660ec373992bc55a12ab2aa0dee923e7bba764 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:53:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: v0.43 table, round 1 (named types; file-private
 helpers; toast types and places colocated)

Commit 19's review (V1-RV-3, V1-RV-4, V1-RV-6). The types the table's parts
read by inference are named in src/features/table/types.ts: CompanionRow,
useCompanionRow's declared return (CreatureSheets no longer imports the
hook's type for ReturnType), with WaitingCompanion for waitingCompanions'
rows; CookbookEntry, the no-sheet button and dialog that CreatureSheets and
NoSheet both took as an inline shape; and ViewSeen, seenOf's declared return
and tableQuery's parameter in place of ReturnType<typeof seenOf>.

Six helpers that nothing imports outside their own file are file-private
again, as they were at the base: shownTurn and sameTurn (utils/end-turn.ts),
edgeOf (chat-log/utils.ts), actingOf (turn-toast/utils.ts), sheetSummary
(utils/header.ts) and countsAsUnread (utils/unread.ts). The toast's step
types (ToastSeen, ToastInputs, CardNext, CardStep), read only in
components/turn-toast, move to its types.ts; places.ts (seatOf,
cookbookPlace, sheetPane), read only by GameTable, becomes
components/game-table/utils.ts; sameGroup, a group-equality rule read by
usePartyOpen, leaves party-urls.ts for utils/party-groups.ts, so that file
holds the party URLs alone.

Types and placement only: no statement changes but the moves, no test file
changes. L0 (related suites, eslint over the changed files) and L1 green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
